  "body": "Closes #1119\nClaim: mac/M1\nAuthor model: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (mac/M1-f1119-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (mac/M1-f1119-review-opus)\n\n**Problem.** In `ComposerLayoutHostedTests.host(...)` the settle loop ends after 150 reads even if the frames never settled; the tests then measured a mid-move frame (Opus round 3 of #1114).\n\n**Cause.** The loop had no post-condition, and \"steady\" compared the frames only, not the card layout.\n\n**Change.** Steady now also needs `box.layout` unchanged between reads, and after the loop `try #require(steady >= 4, \"frames never settled: ...\")`. Test file only.\n\n**Tests.** `ComposerLayoutHostedTests` (6 tests). Temporary uncommitted mutation (card frame offset on every read, so the frames never settle): suite RED on the iPhone 18 Pro with \"frames never settled: ...\" in every test. Without it: green on iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Duo. 5 runs in a row on the 18 Pro under 10 busy loops: 5/5 green (loops killed, none left).\n\n**Device-check points.** None (test-only).\n\nNote (Opus review detail): the mutation moves the frames only; the added `box.layout` comparison has no red run of its own, it can only make the loop stricter (a run red), never let a moving state through.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw",
