   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, mac/M1-f1119-review-opus, 2c7f3714)**: APPROVE — head 2c7f3714\n\nThe change is in one file, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ComposerLayoutHostedTests.swift`, and touches tests only. It covers both points of the Opus round 3 review on #1114: Low 1 and the detail.\n\n1. **Detail**, `ComposerLayoutHostedTests.swift:65`\n   - **Problem.** No red run backs the new `box.layout == lastLayout` check. The mutation in `mutation.log` moves only the frames: `card.minY` grows by about 11 400 between runs, and the layout stays the same. If that check were removed, the mutation run would still fail just the same.\n   - **Why it does not block.** The check only makes the loop stricter, so it can only turn a run red. It cannot let a moving state through.\n   - **Optional fix.** Run once with the layout `line` nudged on each read, and see the suite go red. A note in the PR body is enough; no new commit is needed.\n\n**Checked, no failing scenario found:**\n- **`#require` ends the test red.** `mutation.log` shows the 6 tests and 8 cases red with \"Expectation failed: steady >= 4 ↳ frames never settled…\", one issue per case. So `#require` stops the test before any measurement. The failure is reported at line 73 rather than 70 because the mutation added 3 lines to the test file; `orig.swift` is identical to the head.\n- **No vacuous first comparison.** `lastLayout` starts as `ComposerCardLayout()`, where `text == 0`, and `ready` requires `text > 0`. `last` starts empty, and `ready` requires `.controls` and `.card`. So the first ready read cannot count as steady. Both `last` and `lastLayout` are updated on every read, whether or not it is ready.\n- **The comparison covers what the tests assert.** `Equatable` is synthesised and compares all five stored fields: `top`, `chips`, `controls`, `text` and `line`. `editorHeight`, `textCardHeight` and `cardHeight` are computed from those fields. Test 2 asserts on `top`, which is one of them.\n- **The layout is reported on every device.** `ReplyComposerView.swift:149` sends `onChange(of: measured, initial: true)` with no idiom condition, so the iPad does not hit a new red. CI tests only on iPhone (`ci.yml:175-193`).\n- **No new flake risk.** The 5 runs under load passed in about 2.8 s each, and the green runs on iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Duo in about 3.1–3.3 s. That is far below the 7.5 s limit.\n- **SwiftLint, checked by hand.** No line over 140 characters, the identifiers have at least 3 characters, and `for … where` is used.\n\n**Vérifié:** read the diff `origin/dev-swift...2c7f3714`, the test file, `ComposerHeight.swift:56-98` and `ComposerLayoutProbe.swift`; issue #1119 and the round 3 review on #1114; the logs in `runs-1119/` (not rerun): `mutation.log`, `load1`–`load5`, the two `green-*` logs (simulators identified as iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone Duo); `orig.swift` identical to the head. Not done, as instructed: build, simulator, SwiftLint.\n\nAgent : mac/M1-f1119-review-opus (Opus 5.5). Posted by mac/M1 (Claude Opus 5.5); the detail is noted in the PR body (the layout comparison only makes the loop stricter; no red run of its own).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
